Z||000002||1FST2M6||12-07-2000||08:14 AM||||the real reason they squeek. most people just buy a new belt  when you really need the correct belt. a new one will be fine for a short while.. the pitch on the V's in the pullys is made a certain way so that the side of the V's make the pully turn.. the way most US spec belts are made the V is eiter too wide or too deep thus making the belt stand on top of the pulley or making only the ends of the V touch the center of the pulley V. this causes accelerated wear and the annoying squeel at start-up and under acceleration. Continental and Beck Arnley make the correct belts for our cars. the Goodyear, Auto Zone, Pep Boys, and advanced auto parts brands won't work. NAPA carries Beck Arnley and the continental belt can be purchased at your local Lotus, Dealer. NO they aren't any more expensive you just have to FIND them. Paul Spruell Alfa, Lamborghini, Lotus here in Atl. stock them. they just happen to be the same belt the 88 Esprit use.<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 12-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||12-07-2000||09:23 AM||||Try to roll the belt around and check for cracks.  Needs to be tightened for sure, might be a good idea to replace it if you've put a lot of miles on it.  Colder weather helps it squeal, the steering pump belt on my Regal just started squealing today.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
